 Platform Name: 
GitHub CoPilot (Enterprise)

 Vendor:
GitHub, Inc 

 Business Owner:
Engineering

 Technical Owner:
AI Sceurity Engineer 

 Platform Purpose:
GitHub CoPilot is an AI pair-programming tool that generates code suggestions, autocompletions, and chat-based development assistance directly within the IDE. It solves the problem of developer productivity issues by context-switching, and assisting with debugging. Capabilities include inline code suggestions, natural language-to-code generation, and chat-based Q&A on codebases. It will be used by software engineers, DevOps engineers, and QA automation engineers. 

 Intended Use:
-Software development assistance
-Debugging and error explanation
-Unit test generation
-Code documentation assistance

 Prohibited Use:
-Generating code for production cryptographic or authentication modules without senior security review.
-Uploading regulated data (PII, PHI, PCI) into CoPilot Chat prompts
-Using CoPilot suggestions in safety-critical systems without full human validation
-Bypassing mandatory peer code review for CoPilot-generated code

 Data Considerations:
Permitted Data: Internal source code, non-sensitive technical documentation, public/open-source code references

Restricted Data: Customer PII, Regulated data (HIPAA, PCI-DSS, GDPR-covered data), proprietary algorithms designated as trade secrets

Governance Requirements: Enterprise-level content exclusion policies enforced; training data sharing disabled via enterprise admin settings; data classification labels enforced at the repository level

 Key Risks:
-Data leakage via CoPilot Chat prompts
-Hallucinated or insecure code suggestions
-Intellectual property/license contamination from training data
-Over-reliance reducing developer code comprehension
-Unathorized seat access by terminated employees

 Required Controls:
COP-05: Source Code Exclusion Policy
COP-07: Mandatory Review of AI Generated Code
COP-03: CoPilot Access Revocation on Termination
COP-01: CoPilot Seat Assignments 
COP-06: AI Output Accountability Policy
COP-09: Data Processing Agreement Review

 Human Oversight Requirements:
All CoPilot-generated code must pass human peer review before merge. Code touching authentication, cryptography, or payment processing requires senior/ security review via CODEOWNERS enforcement. No autonomous merge or deployment of AI-generated code is permitted.

 Monitoring Requirements:
-Quarterly access and seat reviews
-Weekly SIEM/audit log review for anomalous usage
-Monthly usage reporting to Engineering leadership
-Annual vendor risk assessment

 Approval Recommendation:
Approve with Conditions

 Justification:
The Platform Assessment confirms strong alignment between CoPilot's capabilities and a clear engineering producitvity need. The Risk Assessment identifies manageable risks (data leakage, insecure suggestions) that are mitigated through enterprise-level content exclusions, mandatory human code review, and audit logging already supported natively by GitHub Enterprise. Given the existing maturity of access control and monitoring infrastructure, approval is appropriate provided the listed controls remain continuously enforced and quarterly reviews are performed.
